course: dictionary
lesson: 7908
title: Rather: a little, or would prefer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rather is a small word with a few jobs. It can mean quite or a little, as in «rather cold». It can mean would prefer, as in «I'd rather walk». Read the words around it to see which job it is doing.
explain: Look at the words next to rather. If it comes after would or I'd, it is about choosing: «I'd rather walk.» If it sits between two choices with than after it, it means instead of: «Compliment effort rather than looks.» Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In a story, the Cat says «I'd rather not», so the Cat would prefer not to do what the King asks. Rather can also correct yourself: «It was cold, or rather freezing» means the second word says it more exactly. Each time, the words around rather give you the clue.
fact: Rather means quite or a little, as in «rather cold».
fact: «Would rather» means would prefer, as in «I'd rather walk».
fact: «Rather than» means instead of, as in «Compliment effort rather than looks».
fact: «Or rather» is used to correct yourself and say something more exactly.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «It was rather cold this morning.» What does rather mean here? | *Quite or a little | Instead of | To correct yourself | Would prefer
exercise: The Cat says «I'd rather not». What does the Cat mean? | The Cat is giving the King a present | The Cat is quite tired | The Cat is sorry it spoke | *The Cat would prefer not to
exercise: «Compliment things people choose, like their drawing, rather than their body or weight.» What does rather than mean here? | *Instead of | To correct yourself | Quite or a little | Would prefer
test: Read «Compliment things people choose, like their drawing, kindness or effort, rather than their body or weight.» What does rather than mean? | Quite or a little | *Instead of | To correct yourself | Would prefer
test: Ella says «It was cold, or rather freezing.» What is rather doing here? | Meaning quite | Meaning instead of | *Correcting herself to say it more exactly | Showing a choice
exam: Which sentence uses would rather to mean would prefer? | Rather cold | *I'd rather walk home | Rather than the bus | It was rather dark
